# Day 10 — keep the Docker build context small and clean.
# WHY: everything here would otherwise be shipped to the daemon as build context, slowing the
# build and risking stale artifacts leaking into the image. The Dockerfile builds the jar from
# source inside the build stage, so none of this is needed.
#
# Day 42 — this is the SHARED ignore file for EVERY module image. All eight services build with
# `context: .` (the repo root, so the whole reactor is in scope) + their own -f <module>/Dockerfile,
# so this single .dockerignore trims the context for all of them.

# Maven build output — rebuilt fresh inside the build stage. Day 17: also match the per-module
# target/ dirs of the reactor (order-service/target, inventory-service/target).
target/
**/target/

# The frontend is deployed separately (Vercel); it has no place in the API image.
frontend/
**/node_modules/

# Version control + local IDE/OS noise.
.git/
.gitignore
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
.DS_Store

# Docs and local-only files — not needed at runtime.
*.md
*.log
*.png
*.html
palettes.html
calendar-prebuilt/

# Don't recurse the Dockerfile/ignore back into the context.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
